. २१; M. १२७. २४;
See दिति, इन्द्र। A ब्रह्मवादिन् and a प्रजापति. A देवऋषि. His sons were नारद and Parvata, as also आदित्यस्, Maruts and Rudras.
१२: Br. II. २७. १०४; ३२. ९८, ११२; ३५. ९२-95: ३८. 3;

. १०५; ७१. २३८; वा. 1. १३८; 3. 2; ६५. ११४.
When दक्ष grew angry on account of his daughter कश्यप drank कश्य, a kind of wine;
१४: वा. ६५. ११५-17.
hence his name; hid योग in a cave;
१५: Br.

(II)--a sage and contemporary of कृष्ण. In- vited for युधिष्ठिर's राजसूय।
1: भा. X. ७४. 9.
Came to स्यमन्तपञ्- caka to see कृष्ण;
2: Ib. X. ८४. 4.
one of the sages who left for पिण्डारक;
3: Ib.

(V)--(काश्यप Havis2ma1n); a son of Bhautya Manu;
1: वा. १००. १०७, ११६; १०६. ३४.
of Vatsa gotra;
2: Ib. ६२. १६; ६४. २८.
a pupil of सूत;
3: Ib. ६१. ५५.
had three आदित्यस् as wives, and out of काम for देवकी took human birth as कृष्ण;
4: Ib. ९६. २३०.
one of the seven sages; अ तपस्वी।
5: Ib. १००. ८२. १००. ९६.

(VI)--(see कश्यप) married thirteen daughters of दक्ष;
1: Vi. I. १५. ७७ and १०३.
blessed दिती with a son capable of van- quishing Indra;
2: Ib. I. २१. ३०-2.
a householder to perform rites in honour of him;
3: Ib.
